@startuml c2-containers
!include <C4/C4_Container>

title rag-pavimentos-mvp: C2 Container diagram

' Proposal. Candidate technologies are listed, not chosen. Each choice goes in an ADR,
' after docs/architecture/quality-attributes.md is filled.
' Modular monolith (CLAUDE.md): one API application holds the modules
' (question answering, PCI data, projects and access, change history). Modules belong in C3.
' All candidates run on any cloud provider or on premises (portability, CLAUDE.md).

AddElementTag("pending", $borderStyle=DashedLine(), $legendText="Decision pending (ADR)")
AddElementTag("assumption", $borderStyle=DottedLine(), $legendText="[assumption]")
AddRelTag("pending", $lineStyle=DashedLine(), $legendText="Method pending (ADR)")

' People from C1, with the use cases each one performs.
Person(airport_staff, "Airport pavement management staff")
Person(pm_engineer, "Pavement management engineer")
Person(district_staff, "District/maintenance staff")
Person(consultant, "Continuum consultant")
Person(data_admin, "Client data administrator")
Person(client_manager, "Client manager")
Person(project_lead, "Project lead")
Person(continuum_admin, "Continuum administrator")

' External system from C1.
' CSV and Excel files are uploaded by people through the web application (UC-05).
' For the funding agency only, the API application also has an automatic connection to this system.
' Its method, and so the direction of the arrow, is pending (ADR 2026-11-23-load-pci-data-by-upload-and-connection).
' Sign-in (ADR 2026-11-23-delegate-sign-in-to-an-identity-service). The client identity providers and
' Continuum's Google Workspace connect to the identity service, not to the containers; they are shown in C1.
System_Ext(idp, "Identity service", "Hosted. Platform accounts with MFA, single sign-on with client identity providers, Google sign-in for Continuum staff. User data kept in the US.")
System_Ext(pms, "Client pavement management system", "Existing client database with PCI records per section and survey year, with coordinates.")

System_Boundary(platform, "Pavement data platform MVP") {
  Container(web, "Web application", "Candidates: React or Vue (TypeScript)", "Runs in the browser. Project list and workspace, question box, project overview and section view, data loading, access management. Serves UC-01 to UC-09.")

  Container(api, "API application", "Candidates: Python with FastAPI or TypeScript with NestJS", "Modular monolith. Checks per-project permissions, answers questions with source rows through validated query plans, loads and validates PCI data, keeps the change history. Serves UC-01 to UC-09.")

  ' Hosted or self-hosted is the decision. With a hosted model API, client PCI rows leave
  ' the platform and the model becomes an external system in C1.
  ' Grounding (ADR 2026-11-23-ground-answers-with-validated-query-plans): the model has no access to
  ' the database. It returns query plans, which the API validates and runs, and it sees only the result rows.
  Container(llm, "Language model", "Candidates: hosted model API or self-hosted open-weight model", "Turns questions into query plans, checks plans against questions (judge), and writes answer text from the rows the API retrieves. No access to the database. Serves UC-01 to UC-04.", $tags="pending")

  ' Client data isolation: see ADR 2026-11-23-isolate-client-data-with-row-level-security.
  ' Data layers: see ADR 2026-11-23-backend-modular-monolith-with-data-layers.
  ContainerDb(db, "Platform database", "Candidates: PostgreSQL with PostGIS or Microsoft SQL Server", "Three data layers as schemas: bronze (loads as received), silver (validated PCI per network section and survey year, with versions), gold (serving tables). Also projects, users, permissions, load jobs and audit log. Client data isolated: shared tables with row-level security. Serves UC-01 to UC-09.")

  ' Not required by phase 1 questions. Justified by the evidence requirement and by PDFs later.
  ' If original files are not kept, this container is removed.
  ContainerDb(files, "File storage", "Candidates: S3-compatible object storage or network file volume", "Keeps the original uploaded files as evidence of each load. Later holds PDFs. Serves UC-05 and UC-09.", $tags="assumption")
}

Rel(airport_staff, web, "Uses", "HTTPS; UC-01 to UC-07, UC-09")
Rel(pm_engineer, web, "Uses", "HTTPS; UC-01, UC-02, UC-03, UC-05, UC-06, UC-07, UC-09")
Rel(district_staff, web, "Uses", "HTTPS; UC-01, UC-04, UC-06, UC-07")
Rel(consultant, web, "Uses", "HTTPS; UC-01, UC-02, UC-05, UC-06, UC-07, UC-09")
Rel(data_admin, web, "Uses", "HTTPS; UC-05, UC-07, UC-09")
Rel(client_manager, web, "Uses", "HTTPS; UC-07, UC-08")
Rel(project_lead, web, "Uses", "HTTPS; UC-07, UC-08")
Rel(continuum_admin, web, "Uses", "HTTPS; UC-07, UC-08")

Rel(web, api, "Sends requests; receives answers, tables and section PCI series", "JSON over HTTPS; UC-01 to UC-09")
Rel(api, llm, "Asks for a query plan, a plan check, and the answer text from the retrieved PCI rows", "HTTPS; UC-01 to UC-04")
Rel(api, db, "Reads and writes PCI records, projects, permissions and change history", "SQL; UC-01 to UC-09")
Rel(api, files, "Stores and reads original uploaded files", "UC-05, UC-09")
Rel(api, pms, "Automatic connection for the funding agency: PCI records", "Method pending; UC-05", $tags="pending")
Rel(web, idp, "Sends users to sign in; receives a signed sign-in token", "OpenID Connect; UC-07")
Rel(api, idp, "Checks that sign-in tokens are valid", "OpenID Connect; UC-07")

SHOW_LEGEND()
@enduml
